WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.868
-Hi, Busy, how are you?

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:04.036
-Hi, Seth. I'm good.
How are you?

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:06.939
-Good. It is wonderful
to see you, as always.

00:00:06.939 --> 00:00:09.742
And I know your entire family
of four

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.411
celebrated quarantine birthdays.
-We did.

00:00:12.411 --> 00:00:14.747
-And I imagine it's harder
for the kids than the adults,

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:17.383
but you did something really
lovely for your daughter Birdie.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.652
-Well, I don't know.
There's a lot --

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.788
Your kids are a little bit
younger, but here in L.A.,

00:00:22.788 --> 00:00:26.792
parents have been organizing
these, like, drive-by birthdays,

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.094
parades, and things.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:31.698
And like, I did not have it
together to do that.

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:35.701
So I sent out an e-mail
asking for some of her friends

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.470
and our family to send videos.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.838
Like, I thought that was cute.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:42.975
But to be honest with you,
the people that she spent

00:00:42.975 --> 00:00:47.613
the most time with over
quarantine are the actors

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:53.152
from "Community"
and "Brooklyn Nine-Nine"

00:00:53.152 --> 00:00:58.524
because she watched both of
those shows pretty much nonstop.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:01.994
So, I happen to, like,
know some of those actors.

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:05.764
So I texted Gillian Jacobs,
who's like a good friend of mine

00:01:05.764 --> 00:01:08.001
and, like, comes to our house
and Birdie knows her.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:13.306
So, when Gillian came up on the
video, I think Birdie was like,

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:14.907
"Oh, it's just
my mom's friends."

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:18.244
And then Danny Pudi
sent a video,

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.712
and, like, Birdie lost her mind.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.114
And then it was, like,
from "Brooklyn Nine-Nine."

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:24.717
She just --
The tears and the screaming,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:28.187
it was everything
that I truly wanted it to be.

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:29.822
I mean, it was incredible.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.557
-We have a video.

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.025
We're just going to show
a few seconds of it.

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:37.263
But as a parent, I mean, this is
really you hitting the jackpot.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.998
I really just want
to tip my cap.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:43.736
-Okay, can I just tell you
that she's a kid

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:47.974
who's been so unimpressed
with me and my career.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:51.844
Like, her entire life has just
been like, "Yeah, whatever.

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:55.714
You're on television.
Fine, okay? Hi, Courteney Cox."

00:01:55.714 --> 00:01:58.384
You know, like, so unimpressed.

00:01:58.384 --> 00:02:02.322
And this was one of my --
I think this is, like,

00:02:02.322 --> 00:02:04.891
my top parenting moment
of the last five years.

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:07.327
I felt like I finally nailed it.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:10.629
And I also put the call out
so wide, thinking that, like,

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.066
if I only got Gillian
to send a video,

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:15.534
it would be totally nice
and fine,

00:02:15.534 --> 00:02:17.437
but everyone sent videos,

00:02:17.437 --> 00:02:21.607
including her two favorite
YouTubers from England

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:25.144
who I just, like,
DM'd on Twitter.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:26.645
I mean, it was wild.

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:29.315
So, yeah, watch her reaction
when it changes.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.717
It's crazy.

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.152
-Hey!
-[ Screaming in excitement ]

00:02:33.152 --> 00:02:36.455
-Happy birthday!
Happy birthday to you!

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:37.523
How you doing, big girl?

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:39.959
-Whoa! What?!

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.560
Oh-ho-ho-ho!

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:42.795
-Truly amazing.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.364
Also, incredibly genuine
from her.

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:47.933
This is not --
You know, I don't think anybody

00:02:47.933 --> 00:02:49.602
could pretend
to be that excited.

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:53.072
Now, you have asked Birdie
to do a little acting.

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.508
You asked her to be
in a music video you directed.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:57.610
-Yes.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.146
-Was she hard to convince?

00:03:00.146 --> 00:03:02.248
-Yeah. I mean,
she's not particularly --

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:06.519
she's very, like -- she's just
into what she's into, man,

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:09.489
and, like, if it's not something
she's interested in,

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.490
you can forget it.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.959
I think that's probably,
like, most kids.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:17.363
But some kids are a little bit
maybe more polite, or, like,

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.097
they'll, like --
You know what I mean?

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:22.201
Or they'll -- like, even just
to show that little clip,

00:03:22.201 --> 00:03:26.539
I went and asked her,
and I said,

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:29.208
"You know who Seth Meyers is?"
And she's like, "Yeah, I guess."

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.677
And then I was like, "Well,
you know Josh." I was like,

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:34.513
"You know he's Josh's brother
and he's got a late-night show.

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:37.016
Can I show that clip?"
And she's like,

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:39.352
"Yeah, I guess for him.
Yeah, that's fine."

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:42.521
Like, you know?
[ Laughs ]

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:46.425
So, anyway,
we've been in quarantine.

00:03:46.425 --> 00:03:49.429
This singer-songwriter
lives in our guest house.

00:03:49.429 --> 00:03:51.497
And so, she is by herself --

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:53.700
I mean, so,
she's quarantined with us.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.935
And her EP came out yesterday --
or not her EP,

00:03:56.935 --> 00:04:00.172
but her new song off her
upcoming EP came out yesterday,

00:04:00.172 --> 00:04:02.542
and she was like, "My label
really wants me to make a video,

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.643
but what am I going to do?"

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:06.312
And I was like,
"Well, lucky for you,

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:11.650
we have iPhones and work in
the film industry."

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.588
So we came up with this concept
for the video,

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.456
and I really just loved the idea

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:21.727
of having Birdie and her little
friend that were staying with us

00:04:21.727 --> 00:04:24.430
as this protagonists
in the video,

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:29.502
and having Sarah Beth Tomberlin
is her name as a singer

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:33.372
sort of following them,
and it turned out so well.

00:04:33.372 --> 00:04:36.542
-It really did. It's so much fun
to watch and listen to.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:39.177
-Thanks.
Yeah, I was really proud of it.

00:04:39.177 --> 00:04:44.250
Marc edited it on his
Final Cut Pro on his computer.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:48.020
I think the label, like, at
first, her record label's like,

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.457
"Yeah, I guess the people you
live with can make this video."

00:04:51.457 --> 00:04:54.594
And then they were really
excited when it turned out

00:04:54.594 --> 00:04:55.928
the way that it did,
and so were we.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:58.163
So, yeah, check that out,
I guess.

00:04:58.163 --> 00:04:59.798
-You also have a podcast.

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:02.601
And, Busy, you have often noted

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:04.970
and addressed the fact
that you love to talk.

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:08.140
This seemed like a natural
conclusion of your talents

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.743
as someone who is naturally --

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.178
-Well, Seth, I thought
it was going to be

00:05:13.178 --> 00:05:14.980
a late-night talk show
was going to be the natural...

00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:16.815
-[ Laughing ] I know.

00:05:16.815 --> 00:05:18.918
-But you know what?
A podcast, great.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:21.954
No, I -- Yeah. I had --

00:05:21.954 --> 00:05:26.025
After "Busy Tonight" ended,
Caissie St. Onge, who's my --

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:29.195
who was my show runner
on that show, and I --

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:32.931
basically, we're going in
a whole new direction

00:05:32.931 --> 00:05:35.768
and we had this whole project
we were putting together.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:39.638
And we sold the podcast as
kind of like a part of that,

00:05:39.638 --> 00:05:41.841
and we were going to take people
on the journey,

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.009
kind of like "StartUp."

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:45.043
I don't know if you ever
listened to that podcast.

00:05:45.043 --> 00:05:46.646
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:51.684
So, we had recorded
hours and hours of stuff,

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:53.719
starting in, like, December.

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:56.021
And the podcast was
supposed to come out

00:05:56.021 --> 00:05:57.390
I think the beginning of May.

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.359
And then, obviously,
the world changed,

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:06.932
and our project was, like,
put on hold indefinitely.

00:06:06.932 --> 00:06:10.402
And I just was like,
"Well, what do we do now?"

00:06:10.402 --> 00:06:11.804
And I took a minute.

00:06:11.804 --> 00:06:15.307
I had to, like, figure out
how to homeschool my kids

00:06:15.307 --> 00:06:16.609
and do all that stuff.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:20.479
And then we decided to,
like, lean into the pivot,

00:06:20.479 --> 00:06:23.449
and we asked Shantira Jackson,

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:26.785
who was one of my writers
and performers on "Busy Tonight"

00:06:26.785 --> 00:06:29.555
to come join us,
and we're talking to people

00:06:29.555 --> 00:06:32.324
about pivots that they've taken
in their own lives

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:35.394
and how they worked out
or led them to the place

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:36.896
where they needed to be.

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:41.166
And honestly, I feel like
at this moment right now,

00:06:41.166 --> 00:06:46.872
we all could benefit from
hearing the stories of people

00:06:46.872 --> 00:06:50.842
who, in their darkest hours
thought,

00:06:50.842 --> 00:06:52.811
"Well, I don't even know
how I'm going to move forward,"

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:55.447
somehow figured it out,
took the pivot,

00:06:55.447 --> 00:06:57.182
and, like, ended up
in a better place

00:06:57.182 --> 00:07:00.787
because we're all being
asked to do that, you know.

00:07:00.787 --> 00:07:03.422
-Yeah, and it's really
a perfect example

00:07:03.422 --> 00:07:06.526
that the podcast is
a version of that, right?

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:08.027
That you had
this different podcast,

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:09.495
and then you ended up
with this one.

00:07:09.495 --> 00:07:12.398
So it's also -- it's nice, both
that you talk to guests about it

00:07:12.398 --> 00:07:15.802
and that you serve as
a perfect example of it.

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:17.736
So, congratulations
on the podcast.

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:19.205
-Thanks.

00:07:19.205 --> 00:07:21.941
-Hopefully, I will see you and
your lovely family again soon.

00:07:21.941 --> 00:07:25.644
-I've probably seen your brother
'cause I've actually seen him

00:07:25.644 --> 00:07:29.081
on the street with his mask on,
walking his dog.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:33.418
So, I probably have seen your
family more than, you know --

00:07:33.418 --> 00:07:35.888
-More than I have.
I would say with masks

00:07:35.888 --> 00:07:39.659
and this hair, I could fully
pull off a Josh right now.

00:07:39.659 --> 00:07:41.460
-100%.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:42.861
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.861 --> 00:07:44.763
I really do think --
I do think, Seth,

00:07:44.763 --> 00:07:47.900
that you should film
your post-COVID haircut.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:49.602
-Yeah, I will.

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:51.404
We'll put that out
for the world.

00:07:51.404 --> 00:07:52.804
-I want to see it.

00:07:52.804 --> 00:07:54.774
Just some online content.

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.041
You know what I mean?
-Yeah, you're right.

00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:57.977
You're right.
I should listen to you on that.

00:07:57.977 --> 00:08:01.414
I should pivot -- I'm gonna
pivot into some online content.

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:03.382
-That's exactly
what you should do.

00:08:03.382 --> 00:08:06.419
Alright, well, I mean, it's
so good to talk to you, always.

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:08.521
-Alright, I'll see you soon.
Thanks, Busy.

00:08:08.521 --> 00:08:10.189
-I will.
Tell everybody I said hi.

